# 21. DEFINITION OF A COMPLETED APPLICATION

PitchArena should be considered functional only when the following complete scenario works:

STEP 1:
A student registers and logs into PitchArena.

STEP 2:
The student creates a startup profile.

STEP 3:
The student explores published challenges.

STEP 4:
The student submits the startup to a challenge.

STEP 5:
The application is saved in MySQL with SUBMITTED status.

STEP 6:
The administrator logs in and sees the new application.

STEP 7:
The administrator assigns two judges to the application.

STEP 8:
Both judges log in and see their assigned application.

STEP 9:
Both judges independently review and evaluate the startup.

STEP 10:
The backend calculates the weighted evaluation scores.

STEP 11:
The administrator reviews the evaluations and makes an official decision.

STEP 12:
The administrator publishes the result.

STEP 13:
The student receives a notification and can view the published result.

STEP 14:
The student can view authorized feedback and continue tracking the startup journey.

STEP 15:
Every sensitive action is protected and recorded appropriately.

Also verify that:
- Students cannot enter judge or admin panels.
- Judges cannot enter student or admin panels.
- Admins have authorized management access.
- Users cannot access records belonging to other users without permission.
- Direct API requests enforce the same permissions as frontend navigation.

